cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the software using the metadata
  below and cite the accompanying manuscript.
title: Count Significance
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Canonero
    given-names: Enzo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7180-4562"
    affiliation: Physics Department, Royal Holloway, University of London

  - family-names: Cowan
    given-names: Glen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8363-9827"
    affiliation: Physics Department, Royal Holloway, University of London

repository-code: "https://github.com/EnzoCanonero/count-significance"
url: "https://github.com/EnzoCanonero/count-significance"

abstract: >-
  Python implementations and reproducible plotting workflows for calculating
  discovery significances and p-values in Poisson counting experiments with
  known or uncertain background rates. The repository implements first-order
  profile-likelihood approximations, higher-order Barndorff-Nielsen r-star
  corrections, reference calculations, and Monte Carlo studies accompanying
  the manuscript Discovery Sensitivity for a Counting Experiment with
  Background Uncertainty.

keywords:
  - statistics
  - particle physics
  - counting experiments
  - profile likelihood
  - discovery significance
  - Asimov data set
  - higher-order asymptotics
